WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:34.980
The red-haired girl, Anne Shirley

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.590
who has come from an orphan asylum,

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:42.830
entered into Green Gables to live
with Matthew and Marilla.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.680
But, in truth they wanted a
boy who could help out.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:53.500
Therefore, Anne would be
returned to the asylum.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.070
Why aren't you dressed yet?

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.180
Oh, isn't it wonderful?

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:28.290
It's a big tree, and it blooms great,

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:32.200
but the fruit don't amount to
much never...small and wormy.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.460
Oh, I don't mean just the tree.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.820
Of course it's lovely.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.640
It blooms as if it meant it.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:44.520
But I meant everything.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:50.960
The garden and the orchard and the brook
and the woods, the whole big dear world.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:56.370
Don't you feel as if you just loved
the world on a morning like this?

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.820
And I can hear the brook
laughing all the way up here.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:04.920
I'm so glad there's a brook near Green Gables.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:09.370
Perhaps you think it
doesn't make any difference to me

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:15.080
when you're not going to keep me, but it does.

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:21.760
I shall always like to remember that there is
a brook here even if I never see it again.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:27.390
If there wasn't a brook, I'd be haunted
by the uncomfortable feeling

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:28.700
that there ought to be one.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.710
I'm not in the depths of despair this morning.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:37.080
I never can be in the morning.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.140
Isn't it a splendid thing that there are mornings?

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:45.460
But I feel very sad.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.950
I've just been imagining that it was
really me you wanted after all

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:54.480
and that I was to stay here for ever and ever.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:58.750
It was a great comfort while it lasted.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:05.870
But the worst of imagining things is that
the time comes when you have to stop.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:10.400
And that hurts.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.790
You'd better get dressed.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:22.470
And never mind your imaginings.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:25.410
Breakfast is waiting.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.500
Wash your face and comb your hair.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:33.070
Leave the window up and turn your
bedclothes back over the foot of the bed.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.340
Be as smart as you can.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.640
Good morning Mr. Cuthbert!

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:27.810
Good morning!

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.940
I'm pretty hungry this morning!

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:36.930
The world doesn't seem such a
howling wilderness as it did last night.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:39.860
I'm so glad it's a sunshiny morning.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:45.020
But I like rainy mornings real well, too.

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.380
All sorts of mornings are
interesting, don't you think?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:50.630
You don't know what's going to
happen through the day

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.020
and there's so much scope for imagination.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.650
But I'm glad it's not rainy today,

00:08:57.250 --> 00:09:01.970
because it's easier to be cheerful and bear
up under affliction on a sunshiny day.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.560
I feel that I have
a good deal to bear up under.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.380
It's all very well to read about sorrows

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:11.380
and imagine yourself living
through them heroically,

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:16.300
but it's not so nice when you
really come to have them, is it?

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.240
For pity's sake hold your tongue,

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:22.560
you talk entirely too much for a little girl.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:27.820
Breakfast's ready.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.240
Thereupon Anne held her tongue
so obediently and thoroughly

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:40.220
that her continued silence
made Marilla rather nervous.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:45.240
Matthew also held his tongue

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.260
but this was natural, so that
the meal was a very silent one.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.130
May I begin keeping them away?

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:12.680
Let me help you wash them.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.520
Can you wash dishes right?

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:16.610
Pretty well.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.620
I'm better at looking after children, though.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.940
It's such a pity you haven't any
here for me to look after.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.900
I don't want any more children to
look after than I've got now.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.490
You're problem enough in all conscience.

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:34.600
What's to be done with you I don't know.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.480
Matthew is a most ridiculous man.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:42.660
I think he's lovely. He is so very sympathetic.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:46.700
He didn't mind how much I talked.
He seemed to like it.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:51.590
I felt that he was a kindred spirit
as soon as ever I saw him.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:57.770
You're both queer enough, if that's what
you mean by kindred spirits.

00:10:58.160 --> 00:10:59.620
Yes, you may wash the dishes.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.300
I've got enough to attend to this morning,

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:07.460
for I'll have to drive over to White Sands in
the afternoon and see Mrs. Spencer.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:13.910
You'll come with me and we'll settle
what's to be done with you.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:25.020
After you've finished the dishes go
upstairs and make your bed.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:25.440
Yes.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:35.630
I'll leave it to you then.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.370
Yes, Miss. Cuthbert.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:04.880
Your bed sheets are badly
done compared to the dishes.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:08.210
That's because I've never slept
on such a comfortable bed.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:20.220
Just slap it like this and it'll be done.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:23.970
Really! Can I try it?

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.790
After that, you can go
to play until noon.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:37.380
Really, Miss. Cuthbert?

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:43.920
Remember to remove your dust and wipe
the mud on your feet before coming in.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:45.780
Yes. I'll be careful.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.200
What's the matter now?

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:45.900
I don't dare go out.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:54.300
If I can't stay here there is no use
in my loving Green Gables.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:59.710
And if I go out there and get acquainted
with all those trees and flowers

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:02.650
and the orchard and the brook,
I'll not be able to help loving it.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:08.420
It's hard enough now,
so I won't make it any harder.

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:13.010
I want to go out so much.
Everything seems to be calling to me.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:17.000
Anne, Anne, come out to us.

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:22.130
Anne, Anne, we want a playmate.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:25.530
They're keeping calling me.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.700
But it's better not.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.690
There is no use in loving things

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:37.000
if you have to be torn from them.

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:42.910
That was why I was so glad when
I thought I was going to live here.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:47.070
I thought I'd have so many things to
love and nothing to hinder me.

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:53.520
But that brief dream is over.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:15:00.400
I am resigned to my fate now,

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:06.290
so I don't think I'll go out
for fear I'll get unresigned again.

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:16.360
Miss. Cuthbert, what is the name of that
geranium on the window-sill, please?

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.530
That's the apple-scented geranium.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:21.870
Oh, I don't mean that sort of a name.
I mean just a name you gave it yourself.

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:23.180
Didn't you give it a name?

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:26.990
May I give it one then?

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.620
let me see...Bonny would do.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:34.440
May I call it Bonny while I'm here?

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:40.730
Goodness, I don't care. But where on earth
is the sense of naming a geranium?

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:46.500
Oh, I like things to have handles
even if they are only geraniums.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.450
It makes them seem more like people.

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:52.460
How do you know but that
it hurts a geranium's feelings

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:54.780
just to be called a geranium and nothing else?

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:59.600
You wouldn't like to be called nothing
but a woman all the time.

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:04.170
I named that cherry-tree outside
my bedroom window this morning.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:08.550
I called it Snow Queen because it was so white.

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:12.910
Of course, it won't always be in blossom,

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:15.590
but one can imagine that it is, can't one?

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.600
I never in all my life say or
heard anything to equal her.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:33.120
She is kind of interesting as Matthew says.

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:37.900
I can feel already that I'm
wondering what on earth she'll say next.

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:42.750
She'll be casting a spell over me, too.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.500
She's cast it over Matthew.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.570
But what is Matthew thinking?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:52.220
Wanting to adopt a girl.

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:37.880
We have to eat early today.

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:46.640
I suppose I can have the
mare and buggy this afternoon?

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:51.710
Matthew I know you don´t want to go,

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:55.270
so, I'm going to drive over to
White Sands and settle this thing.

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:59.200
I'll take her with me...

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:02.630
and Mrs. Spencer will
probably make arrangements

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.630
to send her back to the Orphan asylum at once.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:08.490
I'll set your tea out for you

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:13.100
And I'll be home in time to milk the cows.

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:17.410
Still Matthew said nothing...

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:21.540
and Marilla had a sense of having
wasted words and breath.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:24.450
There is nothing more aggravating
than a man who won't talk back,

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.640
unless it is a woman who won't.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.750
Little Jerry Buote from the
Creek was here this morning

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:09.970
and I told him I guessed
I'd hire him for the summer.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:14.740
Matthew, you said you would
adopt a boy to help out!

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:27.430
Goodbye, Bonny! Goodbye, Snow Queen!

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.310
Mr. Cuthbert, goodbye!

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:38.330
Goodbye!

00:22:56.500 --> 00:23:02.500
Anne's hopeful voice kept
sounding in Matthew's ears.

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:08.000
Why didn't he mentioned to Marilla that
he would keep Anne in Green Gables?

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:13.000
Matthew feels very sad.

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:28.000
That afternoon, Matthew had no spirit to work.

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:32.600
He kept praying and waiting

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:38.200
that Marilla would change
her mind and bring Anne back.

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:53.300
Then, Anne said something
witch shocked Marilla on Their way.

00:23:53.300 --> 00:23:56.100
I've made up my mind to enjoy this drive.

00:23:58.100 --> 00:24:02.080
If I make up my mind to, I definitely will.

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:07.150
I am not going to think
about going back to the asylum

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:09.140
while we're having our drive.

00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:20.130
While going to Mrs. Spencer's,

00:24:20.130 --> 00:24:24.400
Anne tells Marilla about her tragic past.

00:24:24.400 --> 00:24:27.530
Next of Anne of  Green Gables:

00:24:27.530 --> 00:24:30.300
Anne's History.
